{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"96286","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/96286","key":"MC-260335","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"18/Feb/23 7:38 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>Steps to reproduce:<br>\n1. Buy out a villager's stock of any item. (until the red X appears over the arrow in the left sidebar.)</p>\n\n<p>2. Pick up that item with the mouse and drag it over to the 3rd slot in the trading menu.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>3. Ensure that you still have enough to purchase the item if it were in stock.</p>\n\n<p>4. Hovering over the 3rd, now empty, slot, left click as if you were picking up more of that item on the crafting menu.</p>\n\n<p>The trade should still give you the item despite the fact that it's out of stock.</p>\n\n<p>To my knowledge, this only works on stackable items.</p>\n\n<p>UPDATE: I apologize for the lack of thorough testing before submitting. Here's a video of the bug.&nbsp;</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"23/Feb/23 9:51 AM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/126197","id":"126197","filename":"minecraft.webm","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-5.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-5.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-